 To write a C++ program that implements the bubble sort algorithm using minimal memory and avoiding potential errors, you can follow the steps below:
Step 1: Define a function for bubble sort
```cpp
void bubbleSort(int arr[], int n) {
    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
            if (arr[j] > arr[j+1]) {
                std::swap(arr[j], arr[j+1]);
            }
        }
    }
}
```
