 Natural query templates:
------------------------

1. Find {Entity}s that have an average {Attribute} greater than {Value}
   Cypher query: MATCH (n:{Entity}) WITH avg(n.{Attribute}) as avg RETURN n WHERE avg > {Value}
   sample\_triplets: movie, rating, 4.5

2. Show {Entity}s related to {Value} through the relationship {Relationship}
   Cypher query: MATCH (a:{Entity})-[:{Relationship}]->(b) WHERE b.name = {Value} RETURN a
   sample\_triplets: actor, acted\_in, "The Shawshank Redemption"

3. List all {Entity}s that have {Attribute} equal to {Value1} or {Value2}
   Cypher query: MATCH (n:{Entity}) WHERE n.{Attribute} IN ["{Value1}", "{Value2}" ] RETURN n
   sample\_triplets: product, category, "Electronics" or "Home Appliances"

4. Find {Entity}s that have {Attribute} between {Value1} and {Value2}
   Cypher query: MATCH (n:{Entity}) WHERE n.{Attribute} >= {Value1} AND n.{Attribute} <= {Value2} RETURN n
   sample\_triplets: employee, age, 25-35

5. Display {Entity}s connected by a shortest path through the relationship {Relationship} to {Entity2}
   Cypher query: MATCH p=shortestPath((n:{Entity})-[r:*]-(m:{Entity2})) WHERE type(r) = {Relationship} RETURN n, p
   sample\_triplets: author, wrote, book, author1, wrote, book1, ..., authorN, wrote, bookN

Keep in mind that the Cypher queries provided above assume a Neo4j graph database schema. Adjust accordingly if using another RDF or GraphQL database system.

